 "text": "Hi! How's life treating you? About one litre per hour is a good rule of thumb. Are you drinking enough on rides? Pack a bottle at each stop and make a habit of it. Drink a little every twenty minutes or so. If a ride goes longer than three hours, a bar or banana helps. Keep food and water separate, in different pockets if you have to stop for a leak. Most people can get away with it on short ride. But on a long one, your body uses energy faster when you' tired.",
